<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#sapa-inca">Glossary</a> · Term · title</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sapa Inca</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sapa <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca</a>, the 'unique Inca', was the title of the ruler of the Inca state. Believed to descend from the sun god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inti">Inti</a>, the Sapa Inca was an absolute ruler of sacred status, governing the four quarters of the empire from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cusco">Cusco</a>. After his death his mummy was kept by his royal lineage, or panaca, which retained his estates. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atahualpa">Atahualpa</a> was the last to rule before the Spanish conquest.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sapa-inca.jpg" alt="Sapa Inca" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Elemaki · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aguas_Calientes.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
